Code ported from SciPy into zuspecial's own sources
---------------------------------------------------
src/zsp_shim_error.h, ndtri_exp: ported from SciPy 1.18.1's
scipy/special/_ndtri_exp.pxd, (C) Albert Steppi, "distributed under the same
license as SciPy" (BSD-3-Clause, licenses/xsf-LICENSE).
src/zsp_boost.cpp: the wrappers around Boost.Math follow SciPy 1.18.1's
scipy/special/boost_special_functions.h, (C) SciPy developers, BSD-3-Clause.
src/zsp_shim_hyper.h, hyp0f1, hyperu and complex spence: ported from SciPy
1.18.1's scipy/special/_hyp0f1.pxd, _hypergeometric.pxd and _spence.pxd,
(C) SciPy developers, BSD-3-Clause.
src/zsp_wright.h, the Wright omega function: ported from SciPy 1.18.1's
scipy/special/wright.cc, (C) Piers Lawrence, BSD-3-Clause (the notice is in
that file), and scipy/special/_round.h, (C) SciPy developers, BSD-3-Clause.
src/zsp_ccomplex.c, npy_cpow: ported from NumPy's
numpy/_core/src/npymath/npy_math_complex.c.src, (C) NumPy developers,
BSD-3-Clause.
Boost.Math itself is not bundled: it comes from the BH package (LinkingTo).
